<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolt</p><h1 class="enc-title">Plan of Agua Prieta</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1920">1920</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Plan of Agua Prieta was the revolt proclaimed in April 1920 at Agua Prieta, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sonora">Sonora</a>, by supporters of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alvaro-obregon">Álvaro Obregón</a> against President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venustiano-carranza">Venustiano Carranza</a>. Most of the army joined it, and Carranza fled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico-city">Mexico City</a> and was killed in May 1920. It brought the Sonoran generals Adolfo de la <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huerta">Huerta</a>, Obregón and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/plutarco-elias-calles">Plutarco Elías Calles</a> to power.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/plan-of-agua-prieta.jpg" alt="Plan of Agua Prieta" width="320" height="475" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Instituto Nacional de Antropología e Historia (INAH) · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Adolfo_de_la_Huerta_2.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
